lane: queues-api-polish
why: four warts left by a day of adding mechanisms one at a time.
  1. the capacity argument means four different things --
     bounded(n) total, relaxed(parts, each) per part,
     adaptive.bounded(n) per part, bufferChunked(capacity, size)
     counts CHUNKS. A number copied between them silently means
     something else, and documenting each case separately was the
     wrong fix.
  2. two styles in one builder: relaxed(parts, each) beside
     adaptive.parts(k).bounded(n).
  3. MultiFifo and AdaptiveFifo are nearly the same type -- eager
     parts against growing ones -- which is a parameter, not a type.
  4. Drain.Batch is a hard 64 and Source.ChunkSize a constant, both
     put in doubt by today's measurements (asked for 64, got 1.67).
how: put the UNIT IN THE NAME. `each(n)` for per-part, `bounded(n)`
  only where it is a total, `chunks(n)` where it counts chunks. Give
  relaxed the same sub-builder shape as adaptive. Fold MultiFifo into
  AdaptiveFifo behind an `eager` flag and port its tests. Leave (4)
  filed -- it is the adaptive-feed lane, not a rename.
  Nothing about behaviour changes; the gate and the numbers must be
  identical afterwards, which is the check.
